      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T15:53:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Upstream changes would require vendor specific flags in a UAPI that make no sense as part of the common dma-heap interface. The best alternative is to create at least 8 different heaps to cover all the functionality they are relying on a couple of flags for now, but that seems a little unreasonable to me. So I think we should take this to allow vendors to bypass the heap flag restriction where both upstreaming a fix and implementing multiple heaps are not ideal.",
      "parentUuid": "b0c89145_29fb304b",
